- increments are independent;
- each increment has mean zero;
- each increment has variance $2D\Delta t$, where $D$ has units coordinate squared per time.

$$
\boxed{2D(\theta)=\sum_i v_i(\theta)^2\bar r_i(\theta).}
$$

$$
\boxed{
2D(\theta)=
\frac{\sum_i\bar r_i(g_i')^2}
{\tau^2[\sum_i r_i'g_i']^2}.
}
$$

- symmetric weights;
- a stable continuous family;
- the noise assumptions already introduced.

$$
\boxed{J(\theta)=\sum_i\frac{(r_i')^2}{\bar r_i}.}
$$

$$
\boxed{D\ge\frac{1}{2\tau^2J}.}
$$

$$
J_{\alpha\alpha}
\simeq\rho\int d^d c\,
\frac{a^2w^{-2}(\partial_\alpha f)^2}{af}
=\rho a w^{d-2}
\int d^d z\,\frac{(\partial_\alpha f)^2}{f}.
$$

